(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:decoupling \"SHIRO & PICO's writing/i18n lifecycle (episode additions, new-language shotlists) no longer shares a repo, issue tracker, or commit history with ai-gftd-mangaka's render-engine/ComfyUI-fleet/D1-R2-Worker infra churn\", :symmetry \"Ren's Ghost Hacker line and SHIRO & PICO now both have standalone content repos (orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker and orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico respectively), rather than one having a dedicated repo and the other living inside an engine repo's data/ dir\", :future_actor_target \"a future self-sovereign atproto publish actor for this series (com-etzhayyim-tsumugu-style, per ADR-2607011500) has one independent repo to point at\", :deferred_pin_debt \"the superproject's other ~90 drifted child-repo pins remain unadvanced in west.yml after this ADR -- explicitly out of scope here, left to whatever workflow normally owns bulk pin advancement\"}"), (:adr/correction "{:date \"2026-07-01\", :what_was_wrong \"original :problem/:decision framed ai-gftd-mangaka as the (accidental) parent repo and named no intended production engine; pipeline-specs.json in the moved corpus was in fact authored against ai-gftd-mangaka's storyboardFromPrompt (2D panel) convention\", :correct_consumer {:repo \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka\", :why [\"own CLAUDE.md self-describes as \\\"mangaka（manga）の anime 版\\\" -- same team-based production-appview shape, atom is `cut` (shot, time-axis) not page/panel\" \"domain model work -> episode -> scene -> cut (clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc) matches SHIRO & PICO's actual shape: 11-min episodes, VOICEVOX voice acting, OP/ED, motion comic (SERIES-BIBLE.md, episode-01.md) -- not manga pages/panels\" \"12-stage pipeline (script/storyboard/layout/keyAnim/inbetween/colorDesign/finish/background/composite/edit/sound/delivery) is the anime production pipeline this series actually needs\" \"animeka's own test fixture (clj/test/animeka/core_test.cljc) already uses {:title \\\"Shiro Pico\\\" :id \\\"work-shiro\\\"} as its canonical round-trip example -- independent prior evidence this series was already animeka's reference content, not mangaka's\"]}, :unchanged \"the decision to split ghosthacker-shiropico into its own repo is still correct -- the content is engine-agnostic regardless of which engine consumes it\", :followup \"pipeline-specs.json's mangaka-shaped spec is legacy/secondary pending reconciliation to animeka's cut-based model (not done in this pass)\", :landed_via \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico PR #1 (docs/animeka-consumer-note), amending README.edn.edn's :engine-note\"}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "SHIRO & PICO (the global-kids sibling series to Ren's Ghost Hacker, in the same GFTD cyber universe) lives at orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico, not nested under ai-gftd-mangaka/data/" "binary assets for this series (character refs, generated panels, motion comic) are NOT in this repo — they live in the separately-named DataLad dataset ~/gftdcojp/ghosthacker-shiropico-assets (B2 + IPFS), unaffected by this split" "manifest/west.yml registration for a single new project is done via the GitHub Contents API single-entry commit against origin/main tip, not a local edit + full nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs regen, when the local checkout's other child-repo pins have drifted from concurrent fleet activity (regen would bundle unrelated pin advances)" "git fetch showing '(forced update)' on a shallow superproject clone is not itself evidence of a real force-push -- verify with gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/compare/<old>...<new> before treating it as one (ahead_by>0, behind_by:0, merge_base_commit==old tip => false positive from shallow re-grafting)" "CORRECTION (same day): orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka, not ai-gftd-mangaka, is the structurally-correct production engine for this series -- SHIRO & PICO is an anime (work/episode/scene/cut, VOICEVOX, OP/ED, motion comic) matching animeka's cut-based 12-stage pipeline, and animeka's own test fixture already uses \"Shiro Pico\"/work-shiro as its canonical example. pipeline-specs.json's mangaka storyboardFromPrompt framing is a legacy/secondary path pending reconciliation. See :correction below.")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "ghosthacker-shiropico-split"), (:adr/related (vector "CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2606282100-mangaka-render-commons-vs-sip-work-split.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607011500-ghosthacker-sip-atproto-actor.edn" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka/CLAUDE.md" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka/clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico#1 (docs/animeka-consumer-note)")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607011816-ghosthacker-shiropico-standalone-repo"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-01"), (:adr/body "# ADR 2607011816: SHIRO & PICO (ghosthacker-shiropico) as a standalone west-managed repo\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nWhile reviewing Ghost Hacker manga progress, `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka`\n(itself just split out of `ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/60-apps/ai-gftd-project-mangaka`\nthe same day) turned out to hold two unrelated things under `data/`:\n\n- `data/ghosthacker/` — Ren's Ghost Hacker line, style-iteration history\n  (`v5plus`/`v8plus`/`v10`) and lettered/color sample PDFs for Arc 0-1,\n  reusing the engine + world assets that live in this same repo.\n- `data/ghosthacker-shiropico/` — **SHIRO & PICO**, a sibling series in the\n  same GFTD cyber universe (\"information is physical\" / Landauer's\n  principle) but a materially different product: global kids' audience\n  (India / Gulf-MENA), 7+/PG/TV-Y7-FV rating, VOICEVOX-voiced anime shorts\n  rather than manga panels. `SERIES-BIBLE.md` documents it as a \"recovered\n  design\" from session `be34e38d` (2026-06-18), independently conceived\n  from Ren's line and cross-over-linked only at the universe level.\n\nInspecting the actual tracked files (`git ls-files`) showed\n`data/ghosthacker-shiropico/` was materially more complete than its own\n`SERIES-BIBLE.md` claimed (which only documents episode 1 as scripted): a\nfull `episodes/` directory holds all 12 episode scripts plus ar/en/es/hi\ntranslations, and episode 11-12 shot lists exist in 10 languages\n(ar/bn/de/en/es/fr/hi/pt/ta/zh). This is a complete, independent narrative\nasset, not pipeline scaffolding — its natural lifecycle (writing, i18n,\nepisode additions) is decoupled from `ai-gftd-mangaka`'s (render engine,\nComfyUI/fleet topology, D1/R2/Worker infra).\n\nBinary assets for this series (character refs, generated panels, motion\ncomic) were never inside this repo to begin with — `ASSETS-DATALAD.md`\nalready routes them to a separately-named DataLad dataset\n(`~/gftdcojp/ghosthacker-shiropico-assets`, B2 + IPFS), independent of\nwhichever repo holds the text/data corpus.\n\nRen's line already gets this separation: it lives partly in its own\nlong-standing repo (`orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker`) rather than solely\ninside the render-engine repo. SHIRO & PICO had no equivalent home.\n\n## Decision\n\nSplit `data/ghosthacker-shiropico/` out of `ai-gftd-mangaka` into its own\nwest-managed repo, `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`, using the\nexact same mechanical pattern `ai-gftd-mangaka` itself was split with\nminutes earlier (plain copy, single commit, `README.edn.edn` recording\n`:source` + a one-line `:note`, private GitHub repo under `gftdcojp`):\n\n1. Copy all 85 git-tracked files (`SERIES-BIBLE.md`, `episode-01.md`,\n   `episodes/*.{md,ar.md,en.md,es.md,hi.md}`, `episode-{11,12}-shotlist-v2.*.edn`\n   in 10 languages, `character-design-spec.json`, `henshin-bank.json`,\n   `pipeline-specs.json`, `ASSETS-DATALAD.md`) into the new repo root.\n2. `git init` + one commit + `gh repo create gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico\n   --private --source=. --push`.\n3. `git rm -r data/ghosthacker-shiropico` in `ai-gftd-mangaka`, commit, push.\n   Ren's `data/ghosthacker/` is untouched — no code in `ai-gftd-mangaka/clj`\n   referenced `ghosthacker-shiropico` paths (confirmed via grep before the\n   move), so nothing else needed updating.\n4. Register in the superproject manifest (`manifest/repos.edn`\n   `:extra-projects` + `manifest/west.yml` entry, `pin == child repo HEAD`\n   verified: `09cbea7ff5107e41387577a1450213d0c1c734f6`).\n\nStep 4 was done via the GitHub API single-entry-commit method\n(`repos.edn :manifest-workflow :canonical :api-single-entry`) rather than a\nlocal edit + push, for two compounding reasons observed live during this\nsession, not just as a matter of following policy: (a) `git fetch` on the\nsuperproject repeatedly showed `(forced update)` on `origin/main`, which\n`gh api repos/.../compare` confirmed in each case was a false positive\n(`status: ahead, behind_by: 0`, i.e. a plain fast-forward misread through a\nfresh shallow-clone graft boundary — the exact failure mode CLAUDE.md's\nGit-operations section was updated to document during this same session);\n(b) the local superproject checkout's `main` tip kept moving between\ncommands, evidence of a concurrent fleet agent committing to the same\nshared working tree. Editing the manifest files via the Contents API against\nthe current `origin/main` tip (blob-SHA-matched PUT) sidesteps both: no\nlocal 3-way merge, no race with a concurrent writer of the same checkout.\n`nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` was deliberately **not** run to\ncompletion as a write step in this session — the local checkout's ~90 other\nchild-repo HEADs had drifted ahead of what's committed to `west.yml` (other\nfleet work in flight), and regenerating from that transient local state\nwould have force-advanced ~90 unrelated pins in the same commit as this\none-line registration (the \"pin regression trap\" the workflow doc warns\nabout). `west update ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico` was used instead to\nconfirm the new entry resolves and checks out correctly.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- SHIRO & PICO's writing/i18n lifecycle is decoupled from\n  `ai-gftd-mangaka`'s render-engine/infra churn, matching the precedent\n  already set for Ren's line (`orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker`).\n- `ai-gftd-mangaka` now holds only Ren-line Ghost Hacker data\n  (`data/ghosthacker/`) plus the generic render/publish pipeline; no\n  dangling references remain (verified empty before deleting).\n- A future publish actor for this series (the same `com-etzhayyim-tsumugu`-\n  style self-sovereign atproto pattern used for Spirit in Physics, per\n  ADR-2607011500) has a single, independent repo to point at, rather than a\n  `data/` subtree of an engine repo.\n- The superproject's other ~90 drifted child-repo pins were left untouched\n  by this change — `west.yml` still reflects whatever state those repos\n  were in as of the last time someone ran the full generator and committed\n  it. Advancing them is out of scope here and left to whichever workflow\n  normally owns that (or a future dedicated pin-advance pass).\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Leave it nested under `ai-gftd-mangaka/data/`**: rejected — couples an\n  independently-written narrative IP's commit history and issue tracking to\n  an unrelated render-engine/infra repo's churn, and is inconsistent with\n  the standalone treatment Ren's line already has.\n- **History-preserving `git subtree split` / `filter-repo` instead of a\n  plain copy**: rejected for consistency with the precedent this ADR is\n  following — `ai-gftd-mangaka`'s own split from\n  `ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/60-apps/ai-gftd-project-mangaka` minutes earlier\n  was a plain copy + single commit (`README.edn.edn` records provenance\n  instead of preserved history). Introducing a different, heavier tool for\n  this split would break that pattern without a concrete need (no one has\n  asked to `git blame` past ghosthacker-shiropico commits from inside the\n  monorepo).\n- **Regenerate and commit `west.yml` in full during this session**:\n  rejected — the local checkout's other ~90 child pins had drifted from\n  fleet activity concurrent with this session; a full regen would have\n  silently bundled ~90 unrelated pin advances into a one-line registration\n  commit. Used the single-entry API method instead.\n\n## Correction (2026-07-01, same day)\n\nThe original Context/Decision above framed `ai-gftd-mangaka` as the\n(accidental) parent and didn't name an intended production engine.\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker-shiropico/pipeline-specs.json`\nwas in fact authored against `ai-gftd-mangaka`'s `storyboardFromPrompt` (2D\npanel) convention — but SHIRO & PICO is structurally an **anime**, not a\nmanga: 11-minute episodes, VOICEVOX voice acting, an OP/ED, and a motion\ncomic, per `SERIES-BIBLE.md` and `episode-01.md`.\n\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka` (also split from `ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp`\nthe same day, structure mirrors `ai-gftd-mangaka`) is a materially better\nstructural fit: its own `CLAUDE.md` describes it as \"`mangaka`（manga）の\nanime 版\" — same team-based production-appview shape, but the creative atom\nis `cut` (a shot on a time axis) rather than `page/panel`, over a\n`work → episode → scene → cut` domain model\n(`clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc`) and a 12-stage pipeline (script →\nstoryboard → layout → keyAnim → inbetween → colorDesign → finish →\nbackground → composite → edit → sound → delivery). Stronger still:\nanimeka's own test fixture (`clj/test/animeka/core_test.cljc`) already uses\n`{:title \"Shiro Pico\" :id \"work-shiro\"}` as its canonical round-trip\nexample — independent evidence that this series was already understood\nelsewhere in the codebase as animeka's, not mangaka's, reference content.\n\nThis does not change the decision to split `ghosthacker-shiropico` into\nits own repo (content remains engine-agnostic and correctly independent\neither way). It corrects the record on which engine is the intended\nconsumer: **`ai-gftd-animeka`, not `ai-gftd-mangaka`**, is primary;\n`pipeline-specs.json`'s mangaka-shaped spec is a legacy/secondary path\npending reconciliation to animeka's cut-based model. Landed via\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico` PR #1\n(`docs/animeka-consumer-note`), which amends `README.edn.edn` accordingly."), (:adr/decision "{:new_repo {:path \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico\", :remote \"gftdcojp\", :visibility :private, :method \"plain copy of 85 git-tracked files from ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker-shiropico/ -> repo root, git init, one commit, gh repo create --source=. --push (same pattern as the ai-gftd-mangaka split itself, README.edn.edn records :source + :note instead of preserving history)\", :head_sha \"09cbea7ff5107e41387577a1450213d0c1c734f6\"}, :source_repo_change {:repo \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka\", :action \"git rm -r data/ghosthacker-shiropico, commit, push to gftdcojp/main\", :unaffected \"data/ghosthacker/ (Ren line) and all clj/ pipeline code -- zero references to ghosthacker-shiropico existed outside the deleted subtree\"}, :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"added \\\"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico\\\" to :extra-projects, via GitHub Contents API single-entry commit (blob-sha-matched PUT against origin/main tip), not a local edit\", :west_yml \"added one project entry (name/remote/revision/path/groups, alphabetically after ai-gftd-gameka) via the same API method, mirroring the ai-gftd-mangaka entry's shape\", :why_api_not_local \"local git fetch/merge on the superproject was unreliable this session: (a) shallow-clone false-positive '(forced update)' warnings, confirmed harmless via gh api compare each time; (b) a concurrent fleet agent was actively committing to the same shared local checkout, moving main's tip between commands -- editing via the Contents API against the current server-side tip avoids both a stale-base 3-way merge and a race with the concurrent writer\", :verify \"pin == child repo HEAD confirmed (09cbea7... matches gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico@main); post-hoc re-fetch of both files via the Contents API confirmed the entries landed; `west update ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico` resolved and checked out the pinned revision cleanly\", :deliberately_not_done \"`nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs` was run locally to preview but its output was discarded (git checkout -- manifest/west.yml) rather than committed: the local checkout's other ~90 child-repo HEADs had drifted from what's committed in west.yml (unrelated concurrent fleet work), so a full regen+commit would have force-advanced ~90 unrelated pins alongside this one-line registration -- exactly the 'pin regression trap' repos.edn's :manifest-workflow warns about\"}}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-01: 'shiropico は ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico でまとめて' (consolidate shiropico data into its own ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico project), during a session investigating Ghost Hacker manga progress\", :investigated [\"ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker-shiropico/ (SERIES-BIBLE.md, episode-01.md, character-design-spec.json, henshin-bank.json, pipeline-specs.json, ASSETS-DATALAD.md, episode-{11,12}-shotlist-v2.*.edn x10 langs) held a sibling series to Ren's Ghost Hacker, independently conceived (session be34e38d, 2026-06-18), targeting a different market/format (global kids anime shorts vs seinen manga)\" \"git ls-files revealed an episodes/ subdirectory not mentioned in SERIES-BIBLE.md's own file-manifest table: all 12 episodes scripted, plus ar/en/es/hi translations -- the series is materially more complete than its own docs claimed\" \"no code in ai-gftd-mangaka/clj/{src,test} referenced ghosthacker-shiropico paths (grep -rln returned empty outside the data dir itself), so extraction was safe with no dangling references\" \"ai-gftd-mangaka itself had just been split from ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/60-apps/ai-gftd-project-mangaka the same day via plain-copy + single commit + README.edn.edn provenance note -- an immediate, reusable precedent\" \"binary assets were already routed to a separate, independently-named DataLad dataset (~/gftdcojp/ghosthacker-shiropico-assets) per the corpus's own ASSETS-DATALAD.md, so the text/data split had no binary-asset entanglement to resolve\"], :risk \"superproject manifest registration hit two live hazards this session: (1) git fetch showed '(forced update)' on origin/main repeatedly, which could mask a real force-push if not verified; (2) the local superproject checkout's main tip moved between commands (a concurrent fleet agent committing to the same shared working tree), and separately its other ~90 child-repo pins had drifted from their west.yml-committed values (unrelated fleet activity) -- a naive local edit + nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs + commit would have risked losing/misreading history from (1) and bundling ~90 unrelated pin advances from (2)\"}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"leave ghosthacker-shiropico nested under ai-gftd-mangaka/data/\", :rejected_because \"couples an independently-written narrative IP's lifecycle to an unrelated render-engine/infra repo's churn; inconsistent with the standalone treatment Ren's line already has via orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker\"} {:option \"history-preserving git subtree split / git-filter-repo instead of a plain copy\", :rejected_because \"breaks consistency with the precedent this split follows (ai-gftd-mangaka's own same-day split from ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp was a plain copy + README.edn.edn provenance note, not history-preserving); no concrete need surfaced for preserved blame history on this text corpus\"} {:option \"regenerate and commit manifest/west.yml in full this session (nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs with no --check)\", :rejected_because \"would have silently bundled ~90 unrelated child-repo pin advances (from concurrent fleet activity already reflected in the local checkout) into a one-line registration commit; used the GitHub API single-entry method instead, per repos.edn :manifest-workflow's stated canonical path\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607011816: SHIRO & PICO (ghosthacker-shiropico) as a standalone west-managed repo"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))